				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-764027#post-1938258</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-764027/scp-1992-j#post-1938258</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 17 Jan 2014 14:58:14 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>toadking07</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1632267</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p>A single passenger somehow managed to escape the train inside a refrigerator from the train's kitchen. He was also dead.</p> </blockquote> <p>Well then he didn't escape the train now did he? I think it would better communicate what you meant by saying, &quot;A single passenger was found several kilometers<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-994306-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup> from the crash site, having apparently sought shelter in the train's kitchen refrigerator. His body was severely batted and broken, the refrigerator having not saved him from the crash.&quot;</p> <p>Or something.</p> <p>Eh, this one feels a little too reliant on pop culture references, which although they can be funny, they lose their wit as time goes on. PRetty sure I got all the references minus the train full of insects and feces for the sonic on.</p> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-994306-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. Or whatever distance measurement, I'm just making this up.</div> </div> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
